WEBVTT

00:13.767 --> 00:16.647
Hey, what are you doing
out here all by yourself?

00:18.857 --> 00:20.947
[NATSUNAGI] Listening
to the sounds of the waves.

00:22.027 --> 00:24.027
You were sitting here
just listening.

00:24.407 --> 00:25.487
Why not look?

00:26.037 --> 00:27.117
What's the point?

00:28.207 --> 00:29.457
I can't see them.

00:31.747 --> 00:34.587
If that's the case,
why not come during the day?

00:35.537 --> 00:38.047
Of course,
I'd much rather do that,

00:38.127 --> 00:40.127
but wouldn't they find me
if I did?

00:40.217 --> 00:41.337
♪

00:41.427 --> 00:43.677
More importantly,
who are you anyway?

00:44.297 --> 00:46.137
I don't think
we've ever met before.

00:47.177 --> 00:49.927
I was just brought here
not too long ago.

00:50.017 --> 00:52.137
A lot of stuff happened,
you see.

00:52.977 --> 00:54.227
I guess.

00:54.307 --> 00:55.897
-Wanna tell me your name?
-Huh?

00:56.817 --> 00:59.317
The grown-ups have always
called me 602,

00:59.397 --> 01:01.407
so I guess that's my name.

01:01.487 --> 01:02.407
♪

01:08.697 --> 01:09.657
[Siesta gasps]

01:09.747 --> 01:11.457
[Natsunagi exclaims softly]

01:11.537 --> 01:13.117
♪

01:20.167 --> 01:21.467
[Siesta chuckles]

01:21.547 --> 01:23.547
-Nagisa.
-Huh?

01:24.257 --> 01:25.467
[gasps softly]

01:25.547 --> 01:28.097
I think that's a rather
fitting name for you

01:28.177 --> 01:29.517
since you love the sea.

01:30.977 --> 01:32.637
So, what's your name then?

01:32.727 --> 01:34.727
I was never given a real name.

01:35.147 --> 01:36.267
Actually...

01:36.357 --> 01:37.437
What is it?

01:38.147 --> 01:40.607
What I have
is more like a code name.

01:41.447 --> 01:44.237
[♪ opening theme song playing]

03:16.707 --> 03:17.667
[Kimizuka grunts]

03:19.167 --> 03:20.877
[KIMIZUKA] What is this?
Where am I?

03:20.957 --> 03:22.747
-[Natsunagi groans softly]
-Uh?

03:23.837 --> 03:24.917
[NATSUNAGI] Uh?

03:25.007 --> 03:26.547
-[KIMIZUKA] Uh...
-[breathes softly]

03:27.927 --> 03:29.177
[screams]

03:29.257 --> 03:30.177
[slaps]

03:30.797 --> 03:33.757
[grunts] Why in the world
would you do that, Natsunagi?

03:33.847 --> 03:35.267
I could ask the same of you!

03:35.347 --> 03:36.687
In what universe is it okay

03:36.767 --> 03:38.557
to kiss your classmate
when she's passed out cold?

03:38.637 --> 03:39.647
[grunts]

03:39.727 --> 03:41.147
This isn't fair.

03:41.227 --> 03:42.727
[SAIKAWA] Could you two
turn down the volume

03:42.817 --> 03:44.317
so the rest of us can sleep?

03:44.937 --> 03:46.067
[KIMIZUKA] Saikawa?

03:46.487 --> 03:48.567
Wait a sec,
what are you doing here anyway?

03:48.657 --> 03:51.777
Oh? You wanna know
why I'm casually sleeping

03:51.867 --> 03:53.197
next to you, Kimizuka?

03:53.287 --> 03:55.327
You think I'm the one
who'd know better than you?

03:55.407 --> 03:58.207
I don't understand why
you're using that tone with me.

03:58.287 --> 04:00.877
Like, you know I didn't
bring you here, right?

04:00.957 --> 04:03.587
I'm starting to think you really
don't remember anything.

04:03.667 --> 04:04.837
[KIMIZUKA] Char?

04:05.207 --> 04:08.087
We were on our way to visit
ma'am's final resting place

04:08.167 --> 04:10.427
when someone kidnapped us
and brought us here.

04:10.507 --> 04:11.637
[BOTH] Huh?

04:11.717 --> 04:12.887
-Wait, that's right!
-Oh, that's right!

04:12.967 --> 04:14.047
Yes, that's right.

04:14.137 --> 04:15.717
Good grief, you guys.

04:15.807 --> 04:18.347
You shouldn't be so quick
to let your guard down.

04:18.437 --> 04:20.597
-You were kidnapped with us.
-You got kidnapped too.

04:20.687 --> 04:22.557
Sure, whatever. I'm sorry.

04:22.647 --> 04:24.817
-[grunts]
-[all gasp]

04:29.067 --> 04:30.277
[ALL] Uh?

04:32.067 --> 04:33.117
[Kimizuka gasps]

04:34.447 --> 04:36.327
[SIESTA] Greetings.
If you're seeing this video,

04:36.407 --> 04:39.957
then I know everyone
is in place, which means...

04:40.037 --> 04:41.877
Kimihiko Kimizuka,

04:41.957 --> 04:43.497
Nagisa Natsunagi,

04:43.577 --> 04:47.457
Yui Saikawa,
and Charlotte Arisaka Anderson,

04:47.547 --> 04:49.757
are all gathered
in the same room.

04:50.717 --> 04:52.507
-Siesta--
-Ma'am!

04:53.007 --> 04:54.847
[SIESTA] I know
it's been a while, Char,

04:54.927 --> 04:56.757
but I'm terribly sorry.

04:56.847 --> 04:58.717
I recorded this video
a year ago,

04:58.807 --> 05:01.847
knowing full well this day
would eventually arrive.

05:02.307 --> 05:03.307
But ma'am...

05:03.397 --> 05:04.477
[gasps]

05:04.557 --> 05:07.647
Siesta? Is that her?

05:07.727 --> 05:10.447
Now then, none of you
gathered here today

05:10.527 --> 05:12.697
were brought by accident
or chance.

05:12.777 --> 05:15.657
The reason I wanted
all of you here is simple.

05:15.737 --> 05:19.617
It's time to find out
what happened to me a year ago.

05:19.697 --> 05:21.867
What happened to her a year ago?

05:21.957 --> 05:22.997
[Kimizuka breathes uneasily]

05:23.917 --> 05:26.287
I want you to witness
what happened to us,

05:26.377 --> 05:28.917
to walk through every wound
we left behind,

05:29.007 --> 05:31.547
and to learn the truth that
followed me into death,

05:32.007 --> 05:33.217
and then...

05:33.837 --> 05:36.467
I want you to decide
for yourselves.

05:36.557 --> 05:37.677
♪

05:39.267 --> 05:41.017
[KIMIZUKA] And thus began...

05:41.097 --> 05:45.187
a retelling of the three years
I spent with Siesta.

05:46.817 --> 05:49.937
We met 10,000 meters
above the surface of the Earth

05:50.027 --> 05:51.817
aboard a hijacked airplane

05:51.897 --> 05:54.567
and embarked on a series
of incredible adventures.

05:54.657 --> 05:57.947
And while we battled
the secret organization SPES,

05:58.027 --> 06:00.657
we met a strange girl
named Alicia.

06:00.747 --> 06:03.707
But even she wasn't aware
that deep inside of her

06:03.787 --> 06:05.917
she harbored a personality
called "Hel."

06:07.077 --> 06:09.337
Then we headed toward
the enemy's hideout,

06:09.417 --> 06:10.797
determined to follow Hel

06:10.877 --> 06:14.007
or perhaps rescue Alicia
before it was too late.

06:14.087 --> 06:17.717
There, we encountered Seed,
the enemy's ruthless leader.

06:17.797 --> 06:19.807
And so, Siesta began

06:19.887 --> 06:22.217
her final desperate battle
against Hel.

06:23.387 --> 06:26.307
What actually happened
a year ago on that island?

06:27.017 --> 06:29.517
Why is the detective
already dead?

06:31.147 --> 06:32.527
They...

06:32.857 --> 06:33.857
She...

06:34.277 --> 06:35.777
learned...

06:35.857 --> 06:39.987
the one who took Siesta's life
at that time in that place--

06:40.077 --> 06:41.827
-[NATSUNAGI] It was me.
-[gasps]

06:41.907 --> 06:42.947
[cries]

06:44.197 --> 06:46.247
I killed Siesta that day.

06:48.037 --> 06:50.207
I took the person
you cared about most

06:50.297 --> 06:51.457
away from you.

06:52.127 --> 06:53.207
I'm sorry.

06:53.297 --> 06:55.837
No, don't say that.
You didn't kill her.

06:55.927 --> 06:57.547
It couldn't have been you.

06:57.637 --> 06:59.887
It must have been someone else.
[gasps]

07:00.347 --> 07:02.967
[NATSUNAGI] I didn't just
receive a heart transplant.

07:03.057 --> 07:04.427
I stole Siesta's heart,

07:04.517 --> 07:06.637
and now I have to live
with what that means.

07:07.387 --> 07:09.057
The memories of my childhood

07:09.147 --> 07:11.317
and the long days
in the hospital weren't random.

07:11.397 --> 07:13.107
They were fragments of the past

07:13.187 --> 07:15.777
from my time at SPES
bleeding into my own life.

07:15.857 --> 07:16.987
♪

07:18.487 --> 07:20.067
[KIMIZUKA]
She remembered it all,

07:20.157 --> 07:22.827
the truth, the past, everything.

07:23.447 --> 07:26.327
Alicia and the girl
called Hel...

07:26.867 --> 07:28.997
both lay deep within her.

07:29.707 --> 07:32.457
You lost your memory from
being exposed to that pollen,

07:32.547 --> 07:36.297
and not just you,
but also Nagisa and Kimizuka?

07:36.377 --> 07:38.887
You remembered
the whole time though, Char,

07:38.967 --> 07:40.677
-didn't you?
-[CHAR] Yes.

07:40.757 --> 07:42.257
I'm so sorry, Char.

07:42.347 --> 07:43.847
[CHAR] Do not apologize.

07:44.427 --> 07:47.477
I know it's not your fault,
so please don't take the blame.

07:47.557 --> 07:51.357
But still, the truth is...
I just want a little more time.

07:51.817 --> 07:53.857
Oh, of course.

07:54.437 --> 07:55.857
[Kimizuka breathes uneasily]

07:55.937 --> 07:58.067
Everything's fine,
so let's calm down.

07:58.147 --> 07:59.237
[ALL] Mm?

07:59.317 --> 08:00.817
[SAIKAWA] Why don't we
clasp our hands,

08:00.907 --> 08:03.867
relax our shoulders,
and let it all go?

08:04.367 --> 08:07.407
Let's close our eyes,
take a deep breath in, then out.

08:07.497 --> 08:09.327
Feel that blood flowing?

08:09.417 --> 08:11.247
Now, carefully open your eyes

08:11.327 --> 08:13.627
and watch as your blurry vision
clears right up.

08:13.707 --> 08:14.707
[chuckles]

08:15.457 --> 08:16.877
Saikawa...

08:16.957 --> 08:19.007
And after we've
centered ourselves again,

08:19.087 --> 08:20.757
why don't we all have some tea?

08:21.507 --> 08:22.587
Oh, man,

08:22.967 --> 08:25.347
how are you the most mature
out of all of us now?

08:26.467 --> 08:27.467
[all gasp]

08:27.977 --> 08:30.437
[NOCHES] A tea party?
That sounds lovely.

08:30.517 --> 08:32.647
I hope you'll allow me
to join you.

08:33.017 --> 08:34.187
[grunting]

08:34.267 --> 08:36.067
[screams, grunts]

08:36.777 --> 08:39.237
[NOCHES] The next time
you attempt to touch this body,

08:39.317 --> 08:41.907
I will systematically shatter
every bone in yours.

08:41.987 --> 08:43.527
But that's not fair.

08:43.617 --> 08:44.777
[gasps]

08:46.447 --> 08:47.577
It's you.

08:50.657 --> 08:52.167
Siesta?

08:54.087 --> 08:55.997
[birds chirping]

09:02.427 --> 09:05.217
Unfortunately,
I don't have any tea cakes.

09:05.297 --> 09:07.257
Shall we order some
to be delivered?

09:07.677 --> 09:09.177
Kimihiko can pay for it.

09:09.267 --> 09:11.937
Come on now, you don't
have to be so mean to me.

09:12.517 --> 09:16.017
So, does anyone know
where exactly we've been taken?

09:16.107 --> 09:18.227
Of course.
I brought you here to regroup.

09:18.317 --> 09:20.357
This is one of
Siesta's hideouts.

09:21.237 --> 09:23.237
First I'm hearing of it.

09:23.867 --> 09:25.157
♪

09:25.237 --> 09:26.367
[Char exhales]

09:27.617 --> 09:30.287
You really do look
just like ma'am.

09:30.367 --> 09:32.867
Listen here,
I'll only say this once.

09:32.957 --> 09:34.627
I'm merely a robot.

09:35.337 --> 09:38.207
I look like Siesta because
I am a bio-android

09:38.297 --> 09:40.417
created from portions
of her body, memories,

09:40.507 --> 09:42.877
and abilities as they were
before her death.

09:43.507 --> 09:45.297
She even gave me my name.

09:46.257 --> 09:47.677
It's "Noches."

09:47.757 --> 09:50.847
It's hard to believe,
but I suppose I have no choice.

09:50.927 --> 09:53.347
The real Siesta would've
let me rest on her lap

09:53.437 --> 09:56.017
instead of shoulder-tossing me
without warning.

09:56.517 --> 09:58.147
[NOCHES]
I've queried my database,

09:58.227 --> 10:01.107
and the result is
that statement is not true.

10:01.187 --> 10:02.857
You won't even look at me now.

10:02.947 --> 10:04.697
If you were really
modeled on Siesta,

10:04.777 --> 10:06.237
then you wouldn't hate me.

10:06.317 --> 10:08.657
Actually,
that statement's untrue too,

10:08.737 --> 10:11.577
as it's because I'm modeled
after her that I dislike you.

10:11.657 --> 10:14.537
I could've sworn I told you
not to be so mean to me.

10:14.617 --> 10:17.337
Why do those two sound
just like an old married couple

10:17.417 --> 10:18.787
who've been together forever?

10:18.877 --> 10:21.207
They sound more
like a classic comedy duo

10:21.297 --> 10:22.797
with the same tired routine
every night.

10:22.877 --> 10:23.967
[Kimizuka sighs]

10:24.047 --> 10:26.387
Listen, Noches,
I understand that

10:26.467 --> 10:28.927
you're the one who kidnapped us
and brought us here,

10:29.007 --> 10:32.227
which means you must've needed
to talk to us, right?

10:32.727 --> 10:33.637
[NOCHES] Mmm.

10:35.227 --> 10:36.897
[NOCHES] Siesta was thorough

10:36.977 --> 10:40.107
and made many preparations
before that fateful day.

10:40.187 --> 10:42.817
And I was designated
to deliver a complete

10:42.897 --> 10:45.527
and accurate account of
what truly happened to you all.

10:47.867 --> 10:49.827
-Nagisa.
-Huh?

10:49.907 --> 10:52.787
You're the only reason
Siesta's will can be carried on

10:52.867 --> 10:54.367
after her untimely death.

10:54.457 --> 10:56.917
And so,
ensuring that you survive

10:56.997 --> 10:59.837
and are able to attend school
was her last wish,

10:59.917 --> 11:02.087
and the very last assignment
she gave me.

11:02.877 --> 11:05.297
So, on her behalf, I must say...

11:06.757 --> 11:08.337
thank you for that.

11:08.427 --> 11:09.547
[NATSUNAGI] Huh?

11:10.347 --> 11:11.807
I had no idea.

11:15.477 --> 11:16.727
Be straight with us.

11:16.807 --> 11:18.727
I don't get why you'd wait
to tell us the truth

11:18.807 --> 11:19.727
about the past.

11:19.807 --> 11:21.057
What could be the real reason

11:21.147 --> 11:23.187
to hide everything
from us until now?

11:23.277 --> 11:25.607
There happen
to be several reasons.

11:26.147 --> 11:29.527
The first reason I was unable
to inform you sooner...

11:29.617 --> 11:31.447
was because Siesta required time

11:31.527 --> 11:33.657
to suppress the Malign
"Hel" personality

11:33.747 --> 11:35.457
within Nagisa's body

11:35.537 --> 11:37.617
and to stabilize Nagisa herself.

11:37.707 --> 11:39.747
And the second reason...

11:39.827 --> 11:42.127
was that she was waiting
for the four of you

11:42.207 --> 11:44.377
-to truly come together.
-[all gasp]

11:45.507 --> 11:49.087
As for the last reason why?
It's simple.

11:49.757 --> 11:50.967
Seed.

11:51.047 --> 11:52.047
[all gasp]

11:52.347 --> 11:54.177
Throughout the entirety
of the past year,

11:54.257 --> 11:57.427
Seed has refrained
from taking any overt actions.

11:57.517 --> 11:59.017
But unfortunately,

11:59.097 --> 12:01.977
recent observations suggest
that is no longer the case.

12:02.057 --> 12:04.437
And that's where
you come in, Nagisa.

12:05.107 --> 12:06.937
Stopping them is your job.

12:07.027 --> 12:09.027
Wait a sec, my job?

12:09.107 --> 12:10.067
It can't just be

12:10.157 --> 12:11.987
Natsunagi's problem though,
right?

12:12.077 --> 12:14.327
That's technically correct,

12:14.407 --> 12:16.287
but that's not
all there is to it.

12:16.367 --> 12:17.907
There are other factors at play.

12:17.997 --> 12:19.157
You must understand,

12:19.247 --> 12:21.417
her role is far greater
than any of yours.

12:21.877 --> 12:25.757
That's because, as of right now,
Nagisa is the Great Detective.

12:25.837 --> 12:26.967
[Kimizuka gasps softly]

12:27.587 --> 12:29.967
Siesta had not yet
communicated this to you,

12:30.047 --> 12:32.297
so allow me
to clearly state the facts.

12:32.717 --> 12:34.677
Our designated
"Great Detective" is--

12:34.757 --> 12:37.977
That's enough!
If you utter another word,

12:38.057 --> 12:40.267
you'll violate
the Federation Charter.

12:40.347 --> 12:42.017
[NOCHES] I don't care.

12:42.107 --> 12:43.687
You shouldn't either.

12:43.767 --> 12:45.687
They're a part of this, too.

12:48.437 --> 12:49.697
[grunts]

12:50.357 --> 12:51.657
[NOCHES] The truth is,

12:52.067 --> 12:54.737
the Great Detective
is one of the 12 Tuners.

12:54.827 --> 12:57.197
They are the 12 shields
of this world.

12:57.287 --> 12:58.957
Interesting.

12:59.037 --> 13:00.407
They keep the balance.

13:00.497 --> 13:03.327
Dangers arise across the globe
at regular intervals,

13:03.417 --> 13:04.497
often at the same time.

13:05.207 --> 13:07.167
And an international
organization

13:07.257 --> 13:10.667
has secretly drafted individuals
to deal with these crises.

13:11.127 --> 13:13.137
They are called the "Tuners."

13:13.887 --> 13:16.007
There are 12 Tuners in all.

13:16.097 --> 13:19.227
They each have different roles.
The "Phantom Thief,

13:19.307 --> 13:21.727
the Shrine Maiden,
the Assassin."

13:21.807 --> 13:24.477
It's said that one of them
is even a vampire.

13:25.227 --> 13:27.067
That seems like a stretch.

13:27.147 --> 13:31.357
But a year ago, tragedy struck
and Siesta passed away.

13:32.027 --> 13:33.867
That's when the role
of the "Great Detective,"

13:33.947 --> 13:36.987
whose job it is to destroy SPES,
became vacant.

13:37.487 --> 13:39.407
It's likely to be you, Nagisa.

13:39.497 --> 13:41.247
You'd be wise
to prepare yourself.

13:41.327 --> 13:44.747
I think you will be designated
as the next Great Detective.

13:44.827 --> 13:47.707
Of course, it hasn't
been formally decided yet.

13:48.047 --> 13:49.627
However, you have the heart

13:49.707 --> 13:52.417
of the previous Great Detective
beating inside your chest,

13:52.507 --> 13:53.757
and you carry on her will.

13:53.837 --> 13:56.257
You can also master powers
that extend

13:56.347 --> 13:58.927
far beyond the abilities
of a normal human being.

13:59.467 --> 14:02.177
A great many people
would consider that in itself...

14:02.267 --> 14:04.057
more than a sufficient reason.

14:04.137 --> 14:06.147
Siesta appeared
in her body once,

14:06.227 --> 14:07.897
but she said it wouldn't
happen again.

14:07.977 --> 14:11.527
Yes, that's correct.
And so, I ask you once more,

14:11.607 --> 14:14.067
on her behalf
since she's not with us...

14:14.147 --> 14:15.487
-[gasps]
-[NOCHES] Nagisa...

14:15.567 --> 14:17.327
will you promise
to carry on the will

14:17.407 --> 14:19.527
of the Great Detective
as best you can?

14:19.617 --> 14:21.867
Huh? I'm not sure.

14:22.537 --> 14:23.827
[KIMIZUKA] Hold on a sec.

14:23.907 --> 14:25.287
Just hypothetically,

14:25.377 --> 14:27.627
let's say she were to agree
to that responsibility,

14:27.707 --> 14:29.417
what should she do first?

14:30.417 --> 14:32.007
What should she do?

14:35.007 --> 14:38.347
I know, let's have her hunt
for a mistake in the record.

14:42.477 --> 14:44.517
[KIMIZUKA] If Natsunagi
is feeling trepidatious

14:44.597 --> 14:47.307
about becoming
the Great Detective,

14:47.397 --> 14:49.307
she should begin
by examining the footage

14:49.397 --> 14:51.437
from one year ago
that she viewed yesterday.

14:51.527 --> 14:53.147
After finding the "mistake"
within it,

14:53.237 --> 14:54.687
she can choose how to proceed.

14:54.777 --> 14:55.777
[GIRL] Huh?

14:55.857 --> 14:57.527
[KIMIZUKA]
That's what Noches said.

14:57.617 --> 14:58.947
-What's with you, suddenly?
-Yeah, what's the deal?

14:59.027 --> 15:00.697
[KIMIZUKA]
And then she let us go.

15:02.787 --> 15:04.247
[birds chirping]

15:04.327 --> 15:08.207
Unfortunately, we don't really
have any clues to go on.

15:10.837 --> 15:13.297
[yawning]

15:14.467 --> 15:16.217
[groaning]

15:19.177 --> 15:21.177
-[NATSUNAGI] You're kidding me.
-[gasps]

15:21.677 --> 15:23.177
You ate lunch up here all alone,

15:23.267 --> 15:26.017
and then you just decided
to take a nap on the roof?

15:26.557 --> 15:29.227
Lunch tastes way better
when you have a good view.

15:29.307 --> 15:31.147
I'm sure it does,
but that's not the point.

15:31.227 --> 15:33.067
I bet you would've
spent the night at school

15:33.147 --> 15:35.187
if I hadn't come
to get you, right?

15:35.277 --> 15:37.447
Is it that hard
to make some friends?

15:37.527 --> 15:39.947
It's not like I don't wanna
connect with people, you know?

15:40.027 --> 15:41.697
-I just don't know how.
-[exclaims]

15:43.077 --> 15:44.827
Well, you can always count on me

15:44.907 --> 15:46.497
as one of your friends
if you'd like.

15:46.577 --> 15:48.497
I can be there for you
through thick and thin.

15:48.577 --> 15:49.877
So congratulations,

15:49.957 --> 15:52.457
your friend counter has gone up
by at least one.

15:52.537 --> 15:53.707
A cute one!

15:55.507 --> 15:58.377
I've never had a real friend
to count on, so I wouldn't know.

15:58.467 --> 16:00.257
Can't help but disagree, huh?

16:00.337 --> 16:03.307
I don't think I get how you ever
got along with Siesta then.

16:03.927 --> 16:06.177
We never really
did get along that well.

16:06.267 --> 16:08.687
We basically got
into a fight every other day.

16:08.767 --> 16:10.977
Would you say you usually
backed down first

16:11.057 --> 16:12.017
when you guys argued?

16:12.107 --> 16:13.977
Sure, most of the time.

16:14.067 --> 16:15.817
But sometimes
I'd get really stubborn

16:15.897 --> 16:18.397
and refuse to talk to her
for a week at least.

16:18.487 --> 16:19.817
And how'd that work out?

16:19.907 --> 16:22.407
Honestly, it pretty much
always made her freak out.

16:22.487 --> 16:24.277
So Siesta's really
that kind of cute?

16:24.367 --> 16:26.537
But whenever I went
to talk to her again,

16:26.617 --> 16:29.617
I'd catch a brief look
of relief flash across her face,

16:29.707 --> 16:30.707
just for an instant.

16:31.127 --> 16:33.457
And then she'd go back
to looking upset and say,

16:33.537 --> 16:34.837
"Are you that stupid?"

16:34.917 --> 16:37.667
Yep, that's right.
Good work, detective.

16:37.757 --> 16:39.667
You'd get
an A-plus in Siesta-isms.

16:39.757 --> 16:41.137
[laughs]

16:41.427 --> 16:42.717
Good to know.

16:42.797 --> 16:44.547
You look genuinely happy

16:44.637 --> 16:46.507
when you start talking
about her.

16:47.637 --> 16:50.187
She was the only one
you ever really wanted,

16:50.267 --> 16:52.357
the one you couldn't stop
thinking about, wasn't she?

16:53.807 --> 16:55.187
Don't worry about it.

16:55.267 --> 16:58.357
Before I met Siesta,
I was completely alone as well.

16:59.687 --> 17:02.107
You're a nice guy,
I can tell that much.

17:03.117 --> 17:05.407
But that's not
near enough to help me.

17:05.947 --> 17:07.327
No matter what I'm doing,

17:07.407 --> 17:09.537
whether it's talking
to my friends in class,

17:09.617 --> 17:11.457
or listening to you
try to cheer me up,

17:11.537 --> 17:13.457
I can't get that sight
out of my head.

17:13.537 --> 17:15.037
It just keeps coming back.

17:15.587 --> 17:17.957
And it's not like
it's limited to Siesta.

17:18.047 --> 17:19.007
Sorry to keep you waiting.

17:19.457 --> 17:20.297
[NATSUNAGI] I've been
responsible for hurting

17:20.797 --> 17:22.257
so many other innocent people
by my own hand.

17:22.337 --> 17:24.007
She said we should
just go without her.

17:31.767 --> 17:33.187
-Oh, lighten up.
-[yelps]

17:33.267 --> 17:34.937
[stutters] What?

17:35.017 --> 17:36.187
[sighs]

17:36.267 --> 17:37.687
Listen here, Natsunagi.

17:37.777 --> 17:40.397
Don't you dare.
It's still my turn to be mad.

17:40.487 --> 17:42.317
Huh? Do you mean
self-deprecation

17:42.397 --> 17:43.567
-isn't your kink?
-[gasps]

17:43.657 --> 17:46.777
[stutters] I'll kill you twice!

17:46.867 --> 17:47.867
[gasps]

17:48.327 --> 17:49.947
-A long time ago...
-Huh?

17:50.037 --> 17:52.407
...when I was really down
and depressed,

17:52.497 --> 17:54.417
she slapped me on the back,

17:54.497 --> 17:57.707
and reminded me that I'm never
truly alone in this world.

17:57.797 --> 18:00.757
So I vow to always be there
to slap you on the back

18:00.837 --> 18:03.837
when you need it, too,
and to hold your hand.

18:03.927 --> 18:05.137
[NATSUNAGI] Mm?

18:05.217 --> 18:07.347
[grunts] It's not like
running your fingertip

18:07.427 --> 18:09.097
down my back
is some great solace.

18:10.017 --> 18:12.557
You can be as depressed
as you want right now.

18:12.637 --> 18:14.097
You can order takeout

18:14.187 --> 18:16.557
and stress eat
until you almost pop.

18:16.647 --> 18:18.397
Or curse
the unfairness of it all

18:18.477 --> 18:20.897
using as much foul language
as you can conjure.

18:21.397 --> 18:24.147
If that's still not enough
to wash away your guilt,

18:24.237 --> 18:26.197
then I'll carry half of it
for you.

18:26.817 --> 18:29.867
Listen, I get it.
I couldn't save her then either.

18:30.327 --> 18:32.077
I have to live with that.

18:32.157 --> 18:35.917
So, the least I can do is help
carry some of your pain.

18:36.917 --> 18:38.207
Kimizuka...

18:39.087 --> 18:41.207
-Well, uh, you know...
-Huh?

18:41.297 --> 18:42.917
I feel like once I say this,

18:43.007 --> 18:45.627
I'll never escape it,
but here goes.

18:45.717 --> 18:48.927
The truth is, I'm used to girls
being mean to me all the time.

18:50.347 --> 18:51.267
[snorts]

18:51.347 --> 18:53.177
[laughing]

18:53.267 --> 18:55.937
What? Why are you
casually sharing your fetish

18:56.017 --> 18:57.687
like it's a fun little fact?

18:57.767 --> 18:59.397
I'm not some pervert.

18:59.477 --> 19:01.227
I'm literally trying
to make you feel better.

19:01.317 --> 19:02.527
You're trying to cheer me up

19:02.607 --> 19:04.397
by confessing
that you're a masochist now?

19:04.487 --> 19:05.607
That's crazy.

19:05.987 --> 19:08.027
You're way more messed up
in the head than I thought.

19:08.117 --> 19:10.447
-[laughs]
-I was kidding around with you.

19:10.527 --> 19:12.487
That's what I get for trying
to make you laugh,

19:12.577 --> 19:15.077
and that's not actually
my fetish, by the way.

19:15.537 --> 19:16.657
[gasps softly]

19:16.747 --> 19:17.747
♪

19:19.207 --> 19:20.837
[NATSUNAGI] You really are dumb.

19:22.707 --> 19:24.917
Like, the biggest dork
I've ever met.

19:25.377 --> 19:27.007
[cries softly]

19:27.087 --> 19:28.427
Which of us is?

19:31.427 --> 19:33.637
[KIMIZUKA] There, there,
you've held it in for so long.

19:33.717 --> 19:35.057
[Natsunagi gasps]

19:36.017 --> 19:37.387
[crying]

19:40.187 --> 19:42.397
[Natsunagi continues crying]

19:49.657 --> 19:50.737
[Natsunagi exhales]

19:51.277 --> 19:54.117
So, now that you're done crying,
we can get back to business.

19:54.197 --> 19:57.327
We should probably talk about
that "mistake" Noches mentioned.

19:57.407 --> 20:00.287
Do you have any idea
what she might be talking about?

20:00.377 --> 20:03.877
I don't. I've got no clue.
Let's see.

20:04.497 --> 20:07.877
When Siesta was alive,
she said the past was the truth,

20:07.967 --> 20:09.757
but something in it was wrong.

20:10.387 --> 20:12.887
So what does that mean?

20:13.387 --> 20:14.887
I'm curious now.

20:14.967 --> 20:17.137
Is it possible
that Siesta made a mistake

20:17.227 --> 20:18.437
back when she was alive?

20:18.517 --> 20:19.847
But that's weird.

20:19.937 --> 20:21.727
Siesta sounds like
someone who was pretty careful

20:21.807 --> 20:22.937
about getting things right.

20:23.017 --> 20:25.687
That's very true.
We can't waste time,

20:25.777 --> 20:27.397
so let's go talk
to anyone involved

20:27.487 --> 20:29.647
and hope they know more
about what happened here.

20:29.737 --> 20:31.777
There's me and Siesta, then you,

20:31.867 --> 20:34.237
but who else might know
something we don't?

20:34.737 --> 20:36.617
Char, but we have to assume that

20:36.697 --> 20:38.537
if she didn't say
anything pertinent then,

20:38.617 --> 20:40.667
then nothing relevant
must've occurred to her.

20:40.747 --> 20:42.207
Maybe our enemies then?

20:42.287 --> 20:45.087
You mean SPES, huh?
How would you suggest

20:45.167 --> 20:47.257
we go about finding
who to talk to though?

20:47.757 --> 20:48.717
[gasps softly]

20:51.637 --> 20:52.597
[NATSUNAGI] Mmm?

20:53.257 --> 20:54.257
We need Hel.

20:54.347 --> 20:55.307
[gasps]

20:55.847 --> 20:58.057
But Siesta sealed Hel away
inside of me

20:58.137 --> 20:59.637
for a good reason, didn't she?

20:59.727 --> 21:01.557
We're just gonna call her out?

21:02.187 --> 21:04.687
I don't know. Then she'll have
sealed her away for nothing--

21:04.767 --> 21:05.857
-One year.
-Uh?

21:07.227 --> 21:10.567
She spent a full year trying
to change Hel's perspective.

21:11.027 --> 21:12.657
I'm sure it'll be okay.

21:13.657 --> 21:16.157
But still, the thought makes
my skin crawl.

21:16.237 --> 21:17.697
I couldn't help but overhear

21:17.787 --> 21:19.367
-what you were discussing.
-[BOTH] Huh?

21:19.447 --> 21:20.747
[NOCHES]
Allow me to take care of it.

21:20.827 --> 21:22.787
I will summon Hel for you.

21:22.877 --> 21:23.787
♪

21:24.417 --> 21:27.337
So? Why are we looking
in my bedroom?

21:27.417 --> 21:29.587
Because your apartment
was the closest place

21:29.667 --> 21:32.087
where it seemed safe for us
to make a lot of noise.

21:32.177 --> 21:33.927
I don't remember
saying anything about it

21:34.007 --> 21:35.887
being okay
to make a lot of noise.

21:35.967 --> 21:37.177
[Natsunagi breathes uneasily]

21:37.597 --> 21:39.177
[KIMIZUKA] And is it even cool
for a detective

21:39.267 --> 21:40.727
to ask for help from a client?

21:40.807 --> 21:42.517
That seems kind of backwards.

21:42.597 --> 21:45.687
You really
are an idiot, Kimihiko.

21:45.767 --> 21:48.187
Siesta would've been the first
to say.

21:48.817 --> 21:50.437
It's justifiable to do anything

21:50.527 --> 21:52.947
to protect your
client's interests, right?

21:53.027 --> 21:54.157
[gasps]

21:54.237 --> 21:56.117
Yep, that's right.

21:57.277 --> 21:58.657
[footsteps]

21:58.737 --> 22:02.117
Noches, how can I meet Hel?

22:02.207 --> 22:05.667
Tell me, can I really speak
with my other self?

22:09.417 --> 22:10.917
[NOCHES]
There is a simple method

22:11.007 --> 22:12.797
to summon her into that mirror.

22:12.877 --> 22:14.177
[both gasp]

22:16.137 --> 22:17.097
[NOCHES] Hold this.

22:17.637 --> 22:19.717
Now, you will need to stare
at yourself in the mirror

22:19.807 --> 22:21.267
and concentrate.

22:21.347 --> 22:22.887
Why two mirrors though?

22:22.977 --> 22:26.107
There are many sayings
about mirrors facing each other.

22:26.187 --> 22:29.857
For instance, that a pair
of mirrors can summon a devil,

22:29.937 --> 22:33.147
and that they can show you
the past and the future at once.

22:34.197 --> 22:36.027
It's not a difficult task
to master.

22:36.447 --> 22:38.657
If you have a genuine desire
to see her,

22:38.737 --> 22:40.237
you need only to look within.

22:40.327 --> 22:42.037
She'll take any chance
to come back.

22:42.747 --> 22:44.907
So just keep looking at yourself
in the mirror

22:44.997 --> 22:47.747
and imagine what you want
the most coming true.

22:47.837 --> 22:49.747
♪

22:50.707 --> 22:51.747
[Natsunagi exhales]

22:53.797 --> 22:54.717
[KIMIZUKA] Uh?

22:58.677 --> 22:59.757
[Natsunagi gasps]

23:00.807 --> 23:01.887
[gasps]

23:03.347 --> 23:04.267
[Kimizuka breathes shakily]

23:04.347 --> 23:05.767
♪

23:20.487 --> 23:21.657
Natsunagi?

23:24.787 --> 23:26.207
[HEL] It's been a long time.

23:26.287 --> 23:27.417
[gasps]

23:27.497 --> 23:28.827
♪

23:32.417 --> 23:34.167
Here I am, master.
